-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
Add MRC error message display support for VGA Text and Graphics modes

[Feature Description]
Implement ShowProgressBarMessage API to display MRC error messages on
VGA display during memory initialization.
The feature supports both VGA Text Mode 3 (80x25) and Graphics Mode 12
(640x480), providing visual feedback for memory training errors.

Key changes:
- Added ShowProgressBarMessage() API in BaseIGpuInfoLib for displaying
  error messages from MRC Error Key Value Table
- Extended IGPU_DATA_HOB to store MrcErrorKeyValueTablePtr and
  GraphicsMode12FontPtr for message display support
- Implemented VgaGraphicsMode12WriteString() for rendering text strings
  in VGA Graphics Mode 12h with bounds checking
- Added MRC_ERROR_KEY enum in MemoryConfig.h with symbolic error codes
- Created static MRC error table with user-friendly error messages.
- Messages display 2 lines above progress bar with automatic clearing
support

This feature enhances early boot diagnostics by providing clear visual
feedback for memory initialization errors.

